{"type":"message","id":"7820dc93","parentId":"5774e8a5","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:53:28.902Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py` now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")`. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass, including `test_dates`.\n\n- **Why it failed:** the old format string had nothing to match the trailing `Z`, so `strptime` stopped with `unconverted data remains: Z`.\n- **What changed:** inputs ending in `Z` or a `±HH:MM` offset now come back as timezone-aware datetimes (UTC for `Z`). Inputs with no zone still come back without one, so `test_naive` and `day_key` behave the same.\n- **Python version:** `fromisoformat` only accepts `Z` on Python 3.11 or later. The environment has 3.13.5, and I found no project file that sets a minimum version.\n- **What to watch:** callers that compare or subtract a `Z`-suffixed date against a zoneless one will now get a `TypeError`. `fromisoformat` is also looser than the old format, so it accepts things like a bare date (`2026-10-12`)."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":387,"cacheRead":26070,"cacheWrite":818,"totalTokens":27277,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":818}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277604384,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8dZBL4A8MFMcco31Fbh","duration":4517.104665999999,"ttft":4491.6533930000005,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26890,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
